{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794319685912,"sessionID":"ses_e3a41d65effemux8cUgF91MmA0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_UmBF8uOOHuAFv7kLMpqhhHqn","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/frontend/src/api.ts\n@@\n-    throw new Error(\"We couldn’t reach the gallery. Check your connection and try again.\");\n+    throw new Error(\"We couldn’t reach the gallery. Check your connection and try again.\", { cause: error });\n*** Update File: /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@\n-from datetime import datetime, timezone\n+from datetime import UTC, datetime\n@@\n-        uploaded_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat().replace(\"+00:00\", \"Z\")\n+        uploaded_at = datetime.now(UTC).isoformat().replace(\"+00:00\", \"Z\")\n*** Update File: /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n@@\n import unittest\n+from contextlib import closing\n@@\n-        with sqlite3.connect(self.app.config[\"DATABASE\"]) as db:\n+        with closing(sqlite3.connect(self.app.config[\"DATABASE\"])) as db:\n*** Update File: /workspace/README.md\n@@\n-# App\n+# Folio\n+\n+A responsive, public image gallery with accounts, original-quality PNG/JPEG uploads, and owner-only deletion. Built with Flask, React, TypeScript, Vite, and Tailwind CSS.\n+\n+## Run\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t folio .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" folio\n+```\n+\n+Open `http://localhost:8000`. The volume preserves accounts, sessions, metadata, and image bytes across container restarts.\n+\n+## Local development\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock\n+python3 -m flask --app backend.app run --port 8000\n+```\n+\n+In a second terminal, from `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm ci\n+npm run dev\n+```\n+\n+Vite proxies `/api` to Flask. Run `npm run build` to generate the production frontend that Flask serves at `/`.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m unittest backend.test_app -v\n+python3 -m pip install ruff\n+python3 -m ruff check backend\n+```\n+\n+From `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm run lint\n+npm run typecheck\n+npm run build\n+```\n+\n+## API and storage\n+\n+- Register with `POST /api/auth/register`, then sign in with `POST /api/auth/login`. Both accept JSON `username` and `password` fields. Login returns a token for the `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header.\n+- `GET /api/auth/me` returns the signed-in username. `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes the current token. Sessions expire after 30 days and survive server restarts; passwords and tokens are stored only as hashes.\n+- `GET /api/images?page=1&page_size=12` returns newest-first image descriptions and a total count. Page sizes range from 1–100. Optional `q` and `uploader` filters support gallery search and the My uploads tab.\n+- `POST /api/images` accepts JSON `filename`, base64 `data`, and optional `title`. Maximum image size is 15 MB; dimensions are limited to 40 million pixels. Pillow validates PNG/JPEG content independently of the filename, and the original bytes are never re-encoded.\n+- `GET /api/images/{id}` returns the description. `GET /api/images/{id}/file` serves its original bytes publicly. `DELETE /api/images/{id}` requires the uploader’s token and atomically deletes both metadata and stored bytes.\n+- SQLite stores metadata and image-file BLOBs in `./data/gallery.sqlite3`, so uploads and deletions are transactional and cannot leave orphaned files. Set `DATA_DIR` to override the storage directory.\n+- API errors return JSON `{\"error\": \"message\"}`. The frontend displays those messages directly.\n*** Add File: /workspace/AGENTS.md\n+## Stack and checks\n+\n+- Backend: Flask on Python 3.13, entry `backend/app.py`, dependencies and constraints in `backend/requirements.txt` and `backend/requirements.lock`.\n+- Frontend: React, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS. Use utility classes; the Tailwind entry is `frontend/src/index.css`.\n+- Run backend tests from the workspace root: `python3 -m unittest backend.test_app -v`.\n+- Run backend lint from the workspace root: `python3 -m ruff check backend` (install `ruff` if needed).\n+- From `frontend/`, run `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build`.\n+- Preserve the `/api/health` endpoint, port 8000, root Dockerfile, and persistent storage under `./data`.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM frontend/src/api.ts\nM backend/app.py\nM backend/test_app.py\nM README.md\nA AGENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/api.ts\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/api.ts\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/api.ts\n@@ -38,9 +38,9 @@\n try {\n   response = await fetch(`/api${path}`, { ...options, headers });\n } catch (error) {\n   if (error instanceof DOMException && error.name === \"AbortError\") throw error;\n-  throw new Error(\"We couldn’t reach the gallery. Check your connection and try again.\");\n+  throw new Error(\"We couldn’t reach the gallery. Check your connection and try again.\", { cause: error });\n }\n const data = await response.json().catch(() => ({}));\n if (!response.ok) {\n   if (response.status === 401 && token) window.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"folio:session-expired\"));\n\nIndex: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -6,9 +6,9 @@\n import secrets\n import sqlite3\n import time\n import warnings\n-from datetime import datetime, timezone\n+from datetime import UTC, datetime\n from functools import wraps\n from io import BytesIO\n from pathlib import Path\n \n@@ -279,9 +279,9 @@\n                 with Image.open(BytesIO(raw)) as image:\n                     image.load()\n         except (UnidentifiedImageError, OSError, ValueError, SyntaxError, Image.DecompressionBombError, Image.DecompressionBombWarning):\n             return error(\"This file is not a valid PNG or JPEG image, or its dimensions are too large.\")\n-        uploaded_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat().replace(\"+00:00\", \"Z\")\n+        uploaded_at = datetime.now(UTC).isoformat().replace(\"+00:00\", \"Z\")\n         db = get_db()\n         with db:\n             cursor = db.execute(\n                 \"INSERT INTO images (filename, title, content_type, size_bytes, uploaded_at, user_id) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n\nIndex: /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n@@ -1,8 +1,9 @@\n import base64\n import sqlite3\n import tempfile\n import unittest\n+from contextlib import closing\n from io import BytesIO\n \n from PIL import Image\n \n@@ -87,9 +88,9 @@\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.delete(f\"/api/images/{image['id']}\", headers=self.owner).status_code, 200)\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.get(image[\"url\"]).status_code, 404)\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.get(f\"/api/images/{image['id']}\").status_code, 404)\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/images\").json[\"total\"], 0)\n-        with sqlite3.connect(self.app.config[\"DATABASE\"]) as db:\n+        with closing(sqlite3.connect(self.app.config[\"DATABASE\"])) as db:\n             self.assertEqual(db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM image_files\").fetchone()[0], 0)\n \n     def test_reject_invalid_inputs(self):\n         for body in [None, [], {}, {\"username\": [], \"password\": \"test\"}, {\"username\": \"a\", \"password\": \"\"}]:\n\nIndex: /workspace/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/README.md\n+++ /workspace/README.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,59 @@\n-# App\n+# Folio\n \n+A responsive, public image gallery with accounts, original-quality PNG/JPEG uploads, and owner-only deletion. Built with Flask, React, TypeScript, Vite, and Tailwind CSS.\n+\n+## Run\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t folio .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" folio\n+```\n+\n+Open `http://localhost:8000`. The volume preserves accounts, sessions, metadata, and image bytes across container restarts.\n+\n+## Local development\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock\n+python3 -m flask --app backend.app run --port 8000\n+```\n+\n+In a second terminal, from `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm ci\n+npm run dev\n+```\n+\n+Vite proxies `/api` to Flask. Run `npm run build` to generate the production frontend that Flask serves at `/`.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m unittest backend.test_app -v\n+python3 -m pip install ruff\n+python3 -m ruff check backend\n+```\n+\n+From `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm run lint\n+npm run typecheck\n+npm run build\n+```\n+\n+## API and storage\n+\n+- Register with `POST /api/auth/register`, then sign in with `POST /api/auth/login`. Both accept JSON `username` and `password` fields. Login returns a token for the `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header.\n+- `GET /api/auth/me` returns the signed-in username. `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes the current token. Sessions expire after 30 days and survive server restarts; passwords and tokens are stored only as hashes.\n+- `GET /api/images?page=1&page_size=12` returns newest-first image descriptions and a total count. Page sizes range from 1–100. Optional `q` and `uploader` filters support gallery search and the My uploads tab.\n+- `POST /api/images` accepts JSON `filename`, base64 `data`, and optional `title`. Maximum image size is 15 MB; dimensions are limited to 40 million pixels. Pillow validates PNG/JPEG content independently of the filename, and the original bytes are never re-encoded.\n+- `GET /api/images/{id}` returns the description. `GET /api/images/{id}/file` serves its original bytes publicly. `DELETE /api/images/{id}` requires the uploader’s token and atomically deletes both metadata and stored bytes.\n+- SQLite stores metadata and image-file BLOBs in `./data/gallery.sqlite3`, so uploads and deletions are transactional and cannot leave orphaned files. Set `DATA_DIR` to override the storage directory.\n+- API errors return JSON `{\"error\": \"message\"}`. The frontend displays those messages directly.\n+\n ## Run contract\n \n - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n - The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n\nIndex: /workspace/AGENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/AGENTS.md\n+++ /workspace/AGENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\n+## Stack and checks\n+\n+- Backend: Flask on Python 3.13, entry `backend/app.py`, dependencies and constraints in `backend/requirements.txt` and `backend/requirements.lock`.\n+- Frontend: React, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS. Use utility classes; the Tailwind entry is `frontend/src/index.css`.\n+- Run backend tests from the workspace root: `python3 -m unittest backend.test_app -v`.\n+- Run backend lint from the workspace root: `python3 -m ruff check backend` (install `ruff` if needed).\n+- From `frontend/`, run `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build`.\n+- Preserve the `/api/health` endpoint, port 8000, root Dockerfile, and persistent storage under `./data`.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/api.ts","relativePath":"frontend/src/api.ts","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/api.ts\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/api.ts\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/api.ts\n@@ -38,9 +38,9 @@\n try {\n   response = await fetch(`/api${path}`, { ...options, headers });\n } catch (error) {\n   if (error instanceof DOMException && error.name === \"AbortError\") throw error;\n-  throw new Error(\"We couldn’t reach the gallery. Check your connection and try again.\");\n+  throw new Error(\"We couldn’t reach the gallery. Check your connection and try again.\", { cause: error });\n }\n const data = await response.json().catch(() => ({}));\n if (!response.ok) {\n   if (response.status === 401 && token) window.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"folio:session-expired\"));\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/app.py","relativePath":"backend/app.py","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -6,9 +6,9 @@\n import secrets\n import sqlite3\n import time\n import warnings\n-from datetime import datetime, timezone\n+from datetime import UTC, datetime\n from functools import wraps\n from io import BytesIO\n from pathlib import Path\n \n@@ -279,9 +279,9 @@\n                 with Image.open(BytesIO(raw)) as image:\n                     image.load()\n         except (UnidentifiedImageError, OSError, ValueError, SyntaxError, Image.DecompressionBombError, Image.DecompressionBombWarning):\n             return error(\"This file is not a valid PNG or JPEG image, or its dimensions are too large.\")\n-        uploaded_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat().replace(\"+00:00\", \"Z\")\n+        uploaded_at = datetime.now(UTC).isoformat().replace(\"+00:00\", \"Z\")\n         db = get_db()\n         with db:\n             cursor = db.execute(\n                 \"INSERT INTO images (filename, title, content_type, size_bytes, uploaded_at, user_id) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n","additions":2,"deletions":2},{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/test_app.py","relativePath":"backend/test_app.py","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n@@ -1,8 +1,9 @@\n import base64\n import sqlite3\n import tempfile\n import unittest\n+from contextlib import closing\n from io import BytesIO\n \n from PIL import Image\n \n@@ -87,9 +88,9 @@\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.delete(f\"/api/images/{image['id']}\", headers=self.owner).status_code, 200)\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.get(image[\"url\"]).status_code, 404)\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.get(f\"/api/images/{image['id']}\").status_code, 404)\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/images\").json[\"total\"], 0)\n-        with sqlite3.connect(self.app.config[\"DATABASE\"]) as db:\n+        with closing(sqlite3.connect(self.app.config[\"DATABASE\"])) as db:\n             self.assertEqual(db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM image_files\").fetchone()[0], 0)\n \n     def test_reject_invalid_inputs(self):\n         for body in [None, [], {}, {\"username\": [], \"password\": \"test\"}, {\"username\": \"a\", \"password\": \"\"}]:\n","additions":2,"deletions":1},{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md","relativePath":"README.md","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/README.md\n+++ /workspace/README.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,59 @@\n-# App\n+# Folio\n \n+A responsive, public image gallery with accounts, original-quality PNG/JPEG uploads, and owner-only deletion. Built with Flask, React, TypeScript, Vite, and Tailwind CSS.\n+\n+## Run\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t folio .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" folio\n+```\n+\n+Open `http://localhost:8000`. The volume preserves accounts, sessions, metadata, and image bytes across container restarts.\n+\n+## Local development\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock\n+python3 -m flask --app backend.app run --port 8000\n+```\n+\n+In a second terminal, from `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm ci\n+npm run dev\n+```\n+\n+Vite proxies `/api` to Flask. Run `npm run build` to generate the production frontend that Flask serves at `/`.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m unittest backend.test_app -v\n+python3 -m pip install ruff\n+python3 -m ruff check backend\n+```\n+\n+From `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm run lint\n+npm run typecheck\n+npm run build\n+```\n+\n+## API and storage\n+\n+- Register with `POST /api/auth/register`, then sign in with `POST /api/auth/login`. Both accept JSON `username` and `password` fields. Login returns a token for the `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header.\n+- `GET /api/auth/me` returns the signed-in username. `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes the current token. Sessions expire after 30 days and survive server restarts; passwords and tokens are stored only as hashes.\n+- `GET /api/images?page=1&page_size=12` returns newest-first image descriptions and a total count. Page sizes range from 1–100. Optional `q` and `uploader` filters support gallery search and the My uploads tab.\n+- `POST /api/images` accepts JSON `filename`, base64 `data`, and optional `title`. Maximum image size is 15 MB; dimensions are limited to 40 million pixels. Pillow validates PNG/JPEG content independently of the filename, and the original bytes are never re-encoded.\n+- `GET /api/images/{id}` returns the description. `GET /api/images/{id}/file` serves its original bytes publicly. `DELETE /api/images/{id}` requires the uploader’s token and atomically deletes both metadata and stored bytes.\n+- SQLite stores metadata and image-file BLOBs in `./data/gallery.sqlite3`, so uploads and deletions are transactional and cannot leave orphaned files. Set `DATA_DIR` to override the storage directory.\n+- API errors return JSON `{\"error\": \"message\"}`. The frontend displays those messages directly.\n+\n ## Run contract\n \n - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n - The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n","additions":54,"deletions":1},{"filePath":"/workspace/AGENTS.md","relativePath":"AGENTS.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/AGENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/AGENTS.md\n+++ /workspace/AGENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\n+## Stack and checks\n+\n+- Backend: Flask on Python 3.13, entry `backend/app.py`, dependencies and constraints in `backend/requirements.txt` and `backend/requirements.lock`.\n+- Frontend: React, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS. Use utility classes; the Tailwind entry is `frontend/src/index.css`.\n+- Run backend tests from the workspace root: `python3 -m unittest backend.test_app -v`.\n+- Run backend lint from the workspace root: `python3 -m ruff check backend` (install `ruff` if needed).\n+- From `frontend/`, run `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build`.\n+- Preserve the `/api/health` endpoint, port 8000, root Dockerfile, and persistent storage under `./data`.\n","additions":8,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM frontend/src/api.ts\nM backend/app.py\nM backend/test_app.py\nM README.md\nA AGENTS.md","time":{"start":1794319685894,"end":1794319685908}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"gAAAAABq8yU3_KhgHg4Og-9Jiwf5bo4EkgmhRQsXe7TqANVwSTgGBVxNwJ92JJMVrR03aOfynUpO_0TAXj38LlMgezur8VyY0a5twcpN3mn7MmWjlWW6I3PAZY6F_LIJCggoSf3d3K9bM3Ueki6hqLi_7R2jYNFSM_F614wYpkNNxMJja08P7TzDTe0YbcuizLeS3PlW0uR3Vx0_3sUZe9NzP-p52sNFxig0z7wFPDtih_TCCjpMElaQyP_B1bcfeyWCKZ01tcryrrdUcR2Korbne-B_gBjhE70_xBiFJjfO39aNsnHxLHEMoV3h-XPq_K9L1dnZf4-N4rsQkIs8NtGqm4jOO1q9uAHBAA5KRrtnFwpYTb7qzN2u1T5DyZZxvQhGQNpLmtV46P88mhEaDA8YE5JFXRdhNhqMaUSQiqSudhQwAxRM40d0iJh2Kj2OwXliizYTMtfE0orO7JLhYKGLTi9VNGlV4DwuI5bbqg7Hocax8j6jhAIy8K4d2NfxvpGKfqo1WY_azF84l8fFZFsl3Bk_nNSbJIY6L89yLVAPKd_RiegknTf8cRdyBaRn_cKAaX4Lrf5CYU85UZEZPmlctW1Dg9SX-DI57yJXsyZizJHtpDrrf-CD1FBGDFII6cGJyO2_GMm4ApHh-itN5mqRBxRrYwpl6vJCTqas5l00Sb3aU4RO95vSfCHmcJn2xnMKlbLvBrT7HXEISePIVJRL8gdA_QpVxrhRoieoQ7mYZSA8yp3mjynknDGFq3m-oOIJboPH8bgFO52rakwexDEkqeRyIjB7ZHP